## A professional website without the hassle

Not every business needs a complex, fully custom-built website — and not every business owner wants to spend time managing one. Our Managed Starter Website service is designed for small businesses that want a clean, professional online presence that ranks on Google and generates enquiries, without lifting a finger.

From **£20 per month inc. VAT**, you get a complete website package — built, hosted, and fully managed by NC Digital. No setup headaches, no technical knowledge required.

## What's included

- **Professionally built website** Your site is built to look professional and generate enquiries — fast turnaround, no technical hassle on your end.
- **Monthly page additions** Every plan includes new pages added to your site each month. Choose the pricing tier that fits how quickly you want your website to grow.
- **Small changes included** Need to update a price, swap a photo, or change your opening hours? Just ask — small changes are part of the package.
- **Domain included** Your own custom domain (e.g. yourbusiness.co.uk) registered and managed for you.
- **Hosting included** Fast, reliable hosting with SSL certificate and daily backups.
- **Ongoing management** We handle updates, security patches, and anything technical so you never have to.
- **Built to rank** Every page is set up with proper SEO foundations so Google can find and index your site from day one.

## Why monthly pages matter

A website that grows consistently will always outperform a static one. Our Starter tier adds 5 pages per month — 60 new ranking opportunities per year. The Growth tier adds 10 pages a month (120 a year), and the Scale tier adds unlimited pages, so your site can grow as fast as your business does. Each page can target a service, location, question, or search term your potential customers are using.

You choose the topics, or we recommend them based on what people in your area are actually searching for. Either way, your site gets stronger every month.

## Is this right for my business?

A Managed Starter Website is ideal if:

- You want a professional online presence without a large upfront cost
- You want your website to grow consistently without any effort on your part
- You're a sole trader, start-up, or small business that needs to be found online
- You want to get online quickly without dealing with anything technical

It's **not** the best fit if you need to manage your own content day-to-day, run an online shop, or need a fully bespoke design. For those requirements, our [custom web design and development service](/services/web-development/) is the better choice.

## Pair it with local SEO for maximum results

A great website is the foundation — but local SEO is what gets it in front of the right people. We recommend combining your Managed Starter Website with one of our [local SEO plans](/services/local-seo-google-ranking/) to maximise your visibility in Google search results and Google Maps.

Clients who run SEO alongside their website consistently see more enquiries, faster.

## Frequently asked questions

**How long does it take to build?**

Most Managed Starter Websites are live within 5–7 days of receiving your content and details.

**Can I make changes to the site?**

Yes — just get in touch and we'll make them for you as part of your monthly management. Small updates are included.

**What if I want to upgrade to a custom site later?**

No problem. We can build you a fully custom site at any point and transition your domain and hosting across seamlessly.

**Is there a contract?**

There is a minimum 6-month term, after which it rolls monthly. Cancel with 30 days' notice after the initial period.

**Does it include my Google Business Profile?**

Google Business Profile setup is available as a one-off add-on for £50. We'll create and fully optimise your profile so your business appears on Google Maps and in local search results. We also offer an ongoing GBP management plan for businesses that want regular updates, post scheduling, and review monitoring — ask us for details when you get in touch.

